Plot (Chronological, not the same order in the scenes) 
A group of old middle school friends (Renee, William, Iris) getting back together in Cafe Ol’ Days (yes there is a cafe named that). Talk about school life + pressure. Hospital system is joked about but not taken seriously
Renee later reaches out to them and they establish an actual fake set of clinics. Justifies it by saying it helps students in an already unfair system (legacies, donations for acceptance, differences in income and opportunities, etc). 
Hospital system being set up: set of clinics, say like 6 different names/clinics. Sell volunteer hours and hire an adult to answer calls to legitimize the volunteer hours. Fake, random competitions and sell 1st, 2nd, 3rd place. Sell writing recommendation letters from “staff” in those clinics
Montage of them all. Heartwarming (for the viewers, I guess) moments where the ppl from the different schools get along together, say where Stuy kids are teaching LAG kids how to code CSS, LAG kids design the front end of the website with their skills and photoshopping the hospitals onto google maps. Normal school kids help out and all bond. 
Renee becomes slightly more complacent + arrogant and won’t communicate when Iris and William want to learn more about her plan for the hospital system 
Tensions rise, and Iris asks William to do a coup de tat but William refuses and remains passive. Iris has felt left out of the plan by Renee and overlooked as an “art kid” and feels that if she lets Renee continue, it would become too large of a system to still hide. Iris then manipulates Amira who leads it. Cue dramatic scene where they arrange a meeting and everyone votes Renee out. Renee, having been usurped, has her ego tempered. By this time, Renee has applied for colleges (so she has the credentials/records in) 
When Amira and Iris take over the hospital system, they accidentally leak evidence that leads Nicole to begin suspecting the clinics. Could be something like accidentally posting the hospital volunteer opportunities too early onto Blumm’s board and Nicole finds it, clicks it, only to see an earlier ver of the website with the pay to obtain volunteer hours. 
Beginning of Nicole’s informal investigation, where she then finds ppl who bought it or saw the website. (not turning pt/climax yet, climaxis actually Nicole deleting the files) 
Nicole catches Iris and formally interviews. Reports to the school board at this point. (Has not presented yet though). Gets Edmund on board to help investigate (hence why we can get more clips from different perspectives/make the film seem more natural).
A few days later, the first clinic was exposed. Then, the rest become exposed (at least it seems like they’re all exposed, from the interview/files point of view). 
At the same time, Renee, after opening the college decisions, finds out she has been rejected from the school(s) she wanted to go to (gets into her safety tho) and feels like all her efforts in the 4 years and the hospital system were all futile. (No the colleges didn’t know abt the scandal nor did they know abt her being the leader at this time) Breaks down from stress. (Recorded as part of her video journals). 
While Nicole is reviewing case files to get ready to present, she steadily over time learns more about the struggles of the other students and also abt William and everyone involved (including Renee). Renee enters the library or wherever Nicole is reviewing it and pushes a USB file in Nicole’s hands. USB file contains Renee’s pov (date and time stamps included of course) (possibly 3 items, starting with 1: recording herself excited abt Stuy hospital idea in bedroom, when parents knock on her door and shout from outside for her to get to doing hw and focus on getting into a good college like her cousin (Timmy :D) did or something). We want this to be tangible pressure, and we want Renee to wince and then quickly force a smile and say bye to the camera. Also 1.somethings since we need to make it look a bit fuller, a few clips of collab moments/heartwarming parts2: college decisions and her breaking down. This is important, bec it’s part of setting up climax. We need an actor who is able to break down as in laugh and cry at the same time/act out of it, lightly banging on the table so the camera shakes. Can’t be too dramatic, we want it to still be contained here or else it’ll lose sophistication.  3: text note that says something along the lines of “Let it be me. Everyone else wasn't heavily involved. Some people needed this”). 
Nicole, after watching this, pauses, and doesn’t speak (she’s alone rn). Next day, she presents the case but turns out she only reveals Renee and the few ppl already outed. 
Rest, including Wiliam, get out of the stuy hospital team with no consequences (no one knows). Got the money to go to the prestigious college. 
Nicole and Edmund make up very touching
Cut 1 year later, Renee and Nicole meet up. Nicole possibly wants to tie ends or reach out (from mild guilt, since after exposing Renee, she didn’t get into any colleges after being revealed as leader of the scam). Renee reveals to Nicole that William helped her out by securing her an internship. Info gap here: Nicole thinks she knows a lot abt Renee after having watched those clips and wants to mend anything that happened, but Renee knows basically nothing abt Nicole except she was a formal investigator. College admission is an important factor but not defining in life and Renee finds this out after losing friends.
Ending here where Nicole asks something along the lines "maybe....we should meet up for coffee some other time?" and Renee pauses, smiles, and says something along the lines "you aren't obligated. we don't know each other. I don’t think you know me. You saw me, but did you know me? " and then wait for a second or two, turn, and leave. (the last line is essential since we want to tell the audience basically that even this ver isn’t complete, not representative of everything that happened and still biased). Needs to be said in a calm, somewhat bittersweet voice. Matter of fact sort of manner. NO MUSIC 

Yayyyyy cut!!

Side note: 
Plot twist is basically Nicole deleting the important files hiding the rest of the clinics and ppl. 
Audience sees Nicole being morally righteous (WE WANT THEM TO THINK THEY HAVE HER FIGURED OUT). However, at some pt, Nicole has come to the conclusion that it may be better to mitigate the damage at this point, it would only harm other students/do more harm than good. Does upholding fairness matter to that degree if the system is already biased/unfair? Does it matter is she’s right if it still harms so many people who she can understand now? Through Renee, she learns to see William’s side of things and the other realities. Essentially, audience also comes to realize that Nicole, while she might have been seen as objective, was still very much subjective and they don’t know fully in what direction or to what extent. Renee showed to Nicole what she wanted to show through the USB, but even then, Nicole decided what parts of that got shown to the council/school board and from there, Nicole and the audience still don’t actually know Renee; a more intimate scene doesn’t mean full understanding. Also, maybe we want Nicole to learn of Edmund’s involvement and combined with her understanding of Renee, she chooses to hide/prevent it from leaking.


